{"abstract":[{"text":"Convert Markdown files from the terminal and preview the text generators.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingTheCommandLineTools"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"MarkdownKit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Using the Command-Line Tools"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The MarkdownKit package contains two command-line tools. Both are provided to serve as a demo and as a basis for customization to specific use cases, and both are only functional on macOS. The simplest way to build and run them is the Swift Package Manager (SPM), in a checkout of the repository.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Convert-Markdown-files","level":3,"text":"Convert Markdown files","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"MarkdownKitProcess","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Sources/MarkdownKitProcess/MarkdownKitProcess.swift","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" that outputs Markdown content (parsed with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") either as HTML, RTF, RTFD, PDF, or pretty-printed text, including the option to output ANSI-compliant markup. The tool either outputs a single Markdown text file into an output file or, when applied to a folder, outputs all Markdown files within the folder into output files in a target folder. Existing output files are not touched unless the option ","type":"text"},{"code":"--overwrite","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is used.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tool is a thin wrapper around ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": it reads the files, calls ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/text(_:width:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/ansi(_:width:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/html(_:math:safeMode:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/rtf(_:title:author:renderingOptions:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/rtfd(_:title:author:maxImageWidth:renderingOptions:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/pdf(_:title:author:pageSize:margins:renderingOptions:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and writes the result, so you can do the same in your own code, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ConvertingMarkdownIntoDocuments","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["> git clone https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit.git","> cd swift-markdownkit","> swift run MarkdownKitProcess --help","USAGE: MarkdownKitProcess [<option> ...] <source> [<target>]","OPTIONS:","  -f, --format <format>","      Output format: 'text' (plain text, default), 'ansi' (text marked up with ANSI escape codes), 'html', 'rtf', 'rtfd', or 'pdf'.","  -w, --width <columns>","      Width in columns of the formats 'text' and 'ansi', at least 10 (default: the width of the terminal, or 80).","  -p, --page <size>","      Size of the pages of the format 'pdf': 'a4' (default), 'letter', or '<width>x<height>' in points, or with a unit ('pt', 'in', 'mm' or 'cm'), e.g. '210x297mm'.","  -m, --margins <widths>","      Margins of the pages of the format 'pdf', in points or with a unit ('pt', 'in', 'mm' or 'cm'): one width for all sides, two for top and bottom and for left and right, or four for top, right, bottom and left, e.g. '20mm 15mm' (default: '1in').","  -o, --overwrite","      Replaces output files which already exist. Without this option, they are not touched.","  -h, --help","      Prints this usage description.","PARAMETERS:","  <source>","      A Markdown file, or a directory of Markdown files (the files ending in '.md').","  <target>","      The file, or the directory into which the converted files are written. The converted","      file of 'a.md' is called 'a.txt' ('text' and 'ansi'), 'a.html', 'a.rtf', 'a.rtfd' or","      'a.pdf'. '-' prints the output (not possible for 'rtfd' and 'pdf'). If there is no","      target, the converted files are written next to the source files.","Diagrams in fenced code blocks with language 'mermaid' are drawn in the formats 'rtfd' and","'pdf'. Formulas (LaTeX between '$' or '$$', between '\\(' and '\\)' or '\\[' and '\\]', or in","fenced code blocks with language 'math') are typeset in the formats 'rtfd' and 'pdf' (as","images) and 'html' (as MathML). RTF files cannot contain images: the format 'rtf' shows the","code of a diagram and the LaTeX of a formula, as do the formats 'text' and 'ansi'."],"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Include-diagrams","level":3,"text":"Include diagrams","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The formats ","type":"text"},{"code":"rtfd","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"pdf","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" include ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://mermaid.js.org","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" diagrams (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") and formulas (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MathematicalFormulas","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") as images, and the format ","type":"text"},{"code":"html","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" typesets formulas as MathML, which browsers display without a style sheet or fonts. RTF files cannot contain the images that ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSAttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" creates, so the format ","type":"text"},{"code":"rtf","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shows the code of a diagram and the LaTeX of a formula instead, like the formats ","type":"text"},{"code":"text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ansi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The images of an RTFD document are in the files ","type":"text"},{"code":"Image 1.png","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Formula 1.png","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and so on, and a formula within a line is aligned with the text. The directory ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Examples/Demo.md","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" contains a Markdown file with the demo document of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"MarkdownViewer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sample app, including two diagrams, for trying the tool: The pages of the format ","type":"text"},{"code":"pdf","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are A4 with margins of one inch, unless ","type":"text"},{"code":"--page","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"--margins","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" say otherwise: ","type":"text"},{"code":"--page letter --margins 20mm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for US Letter with margins of 20 millimeters, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"--page 210x297mm --margins \"25mm 20mm\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a size and margins of your own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["> swift run MarkdownKitProcess --format rtfd Examples/Demo.md /tmp/Demo.rtfd","converted 'Demo.md' into 'Demo.rtfd'","> swift run MarkdownKitProcess --format rtfd Examples/Demo.md /tmp/Demo.rtfd","error: '/tmp/Demo.rtfd' already exists (use --overwrite to replace it)","> swift run MarkdownKitProcess --format rtfd --overwrite Examples/Demo.md /tmp/Demo.rtfd","converted 'Demo.md' into 'Demo.rtfd'"],"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Preview-the-text-generators","level":3,"text":"Preview the text generators","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A second tool, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit/blob/master/Sources/MarkdownTermViewer/main.swift","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", does not read any files. It prints a demo document with the features of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (the document displayed by the ","type":"text"},{"code":"MarkdownViewer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sample app: formatted text, tables, task lists, code blocks, …) either as plain text (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/StringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") or marked up with ANSI escape codes (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TerminalGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). This is a quick way to see what the text generators produce:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["> swift run MarkdownTermViewer --help","USAGE: MarkdownTermViewer [<option> ...]","OPTIONS:","  -f, --format <format>","      Output format: 'text' (plain text, default) or 'ansi' (marked up with ANSI escape codes).","  -w, --width <columns>","      Width in columns, at least 10 (default: the width of the terminal, or 80).","  -h, --help","      Prints this usage description.","> swift run MarkdownTermViewer --format ansi --width 60"],"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The output of ","type":"text"},{"code":"--format ansi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is only rendered correctly by a terminal. Xcode’s console shows the escape sequences as raw characters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse, process and display text in Markdown format.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"MarkdownKit","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ConvertingMarkdownIntoDocuments":{"abstract":[{"text":"Turn a Markdown document into text, HTML, RTF, RTFD or PDF with one call.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ConvertingMarkdownIntoDocuments","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Converting Markdown into Documents","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/convertingmarkdownintodocuments"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams":{"abstract":[{"text":"Show fenced code blocks with the language ","type":"text"},{"code":"mermaid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as diagrams in attributed strings.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Drawing Mermaid Diagrams","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/drawingmermaiddiagrams"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser":{"abstract":[{"code":"FullMarkdownParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects are used to parse Markdown text represented as a string using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"all features of MarkdownKit: the syntax of the CommonMark specification and all extensions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that MarkdownKit implements.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FullMarkdownParser"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FullMarkdownParser"}],"role":"symbol","title":"FullMarkdownParser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/fullmarkdownparser"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput":{"abstract":[{"text":"Convert a parsed Markdown document into HTML, attributed strings, plain text or text for ANSI terminals.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Generating Output","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/generatingoutput"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingTerminalOutput":{"abstract":[{"text":"Format Markdown documents as plain text, or as text with ANSI styling for terminals.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingTerminalOutput","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Generating Plain Text and Terminal Output","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/generatingterminaloutput"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil":{"abstract":[{"code":"MarkdownUtil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the place to start if you want to use MarkdownKit for a task without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assembling parsers and generators yourself. It has two groups of methods:","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MarkdownUtil"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MarkdownUtil"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MarkdownUtil","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/markdownutil"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/ansi(_:width:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns the document as text which is marked up with ANSI escape codes (colors, bold and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"italic text, …), formatted for lines of ","type":"text"},{"code":"width","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" columns (at least 10), so that an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ANSI-compliant terminal shows it formatted. Diagrams are shown as code and formulas as they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"were written. This method is available on all platforms.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ansi"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit5BlockO","text":"Block"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"width"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/ansi(_:width:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"ansi(_:width:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/markdownutil/ansi(_:width:)"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/html(_:math:safeMode:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns the document as HTML. Formulas are typeset (by KaTeX) as MathML, which browsers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"display without a style sheet or fonts; use ","type":"text"},{"code":"math","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to select another form. This method is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"available on all platforms, but KaTeX does not run on watchOS: formulas are written with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delimiters there.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"html"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit5BlockO","text":"Block"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"math"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit17MathHtmlGeneratorC","text":"MathHtmlGenerator"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit17MathHtmlGeneratorC6OutputO","text":"Output"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"safeMode"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/html(_:math:safeMode:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"html(_:math:safeMode:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/markdownutil/html(_:math:safemode:)"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/pdf(_:title:author:pageSize:margins:renderingOptions:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns the document as a PDF document: the content of a ","type":"text"},{"code":".pdf","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file. The text, lists,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tables, quotes and code blocks are laid out as they are in a text view, in the width of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the pages, and are broken into pages. Diagrams (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"formulas (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MathematicalFormulas","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") are drawn as images. All diagrams are scaled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alike, so that a diagram of the width of a page for which Mermaid draws (800 points)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fills the text of a page; formulas are scaled down if they are wider than the text.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The numbers and bullets of lists sit on the baseline of the first line of their items.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Links are clickable (except those to a place in the same document, ","type":"text"},{"code":"#name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"pdf"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit5BlockO","text":"Block"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"title"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"author"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"pageSize"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@S@CGSize","text":"CGSize"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"margins"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit0A4UtilV6InsetsV","text":"Insets"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"renderingOptions"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC16RenderingOptionsV","text":"RenderingOptions"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4DataV","text":"Data"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/pdf(_:title:author:pageSize:margins:renderingOptions:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"pdf(_:title:author:pageSize:margins:renderingOptions:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/markdownutil/pdf(_:title:author:pagesize:margins:renderingoptions:)"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/rtf(_:title:author:renderingOptions:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns the document as an RTF document. RTF files cannot contain images, so diagrams are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shown as code and formulas as they were written; use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/rtfd(_:title:author:maxImageWidth:renderingOptions:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a document with images.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The result is the content of an ","type":"text"},{"code":".rtf","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"rtf"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit5BlockO","text":"Block"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"title"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"author"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"renderingOptions"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC16RenderingOptionsV","text":"RenderingOptions"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4DataV","text":"Data"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/rtf(_:title:author:renderingOptions:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"rtf(_:title:author:renderingOptions:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/markdownutil/rtf(_:title:author:renderingoptions:)"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/rtfd(_:title:author:maxImageWidth:renderingOptions:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns the document as an RTFD document: a file package, which contains the text and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"images, which is the content of an ","type":"text"},{"code":".rtfd","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directory (write it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileWrapper.write(to:options:originalContentsURL:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Diagrams (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") and formulas (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MathematicalFormulas","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are drawn as images, in files that are called ","type":"text"},{"code":"Image 1.png","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Formula 1.png","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"rtfd"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit5BlockO","text":"Block"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"title"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"author"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxImageWidth"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14CoreFoundation7CGFloatV","text":"CGFloat"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"renderingOptions"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit25AttributedStringGeneratorC16RenderingOptionsV","text":"RenderingOptions"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> sending "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)NSFileWrapper","text":"FileWrapper"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/rtfd(_:title:author:maxImageWidth:renderingOptions:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"rtfd(_:title:author:maxImageWidth:renderingOptions:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/markdownutil/rtfd(_:title:author:maximagewidth:renderingoptions:)"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/text(_:width:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns the document as plain text, formatted for lines of ","type":"text"},{"code":"width","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" columns (at least 10).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Diagrams are shown as code and formulas as they were written. This method is available on all